ity. Other words, such as \"unpleasure,\" are formed in ways that don't quite work. Next, make a list of the words you're unsure about, check each one in a dictionary, and replace them with more precise terms.","rationale":"Word choice is mostly general and several words are misused or non-standard. Precise words such as \"kidnapped\" and \"murdered\" appear, which keeps this from limited.","suggestedLevel":"l2","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"it moderates them to be a better humans being with molarity without having any criminal records"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"It shapes their morals and erases all their bad behaviors that makes others feel unpleasure."}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"phraseology","observation":"Some fixed expressions aren't quite standard English, such as \"put an end on\" and \"pay attention on.\" You also use \"keep ... out of trouble\" correctly, which is a strength. Next, check the prepositions in your collocations, using a learner dictionary to confirm the standard forms, such as \"put an end to\" and \"pay attention to.\"","rationale":"Collocations like \"pay attention on\" and \"put an end on\" show a need for standard prepositional patterns. Correct idiomatic phrases also appear, which supports level 2 over level 1.","suggestedLevel":"l2","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"to put an end on any illegal act that is commited by teenagers"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"This is an important issue to pay attention on"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"grammar","observation":"You often use singular verbs with plural subjects or the wrong verb form after modal verbs, as in \"if the curfews is adopted then they should be obey to this law.\" Next, go through your essay and check each subject-verb pair, and check that the verb after \"should\" is in its base form.","rationale":"Errors in agreement and verb forms occur frequently across the essay, including \"the curfews is\" and \"should be obey\". Errors recur throughout, so the work sits at limited.","suggestedLevel":"l2","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"Therefore, if the curfews is adopted then they should be obey to this law in order to avoid"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"I had a thinking that what if a city council adopts"}],"uncertainty":"low"},{"criterionId":"conventions","observation":"Many words are misspelled, such as \"Unfortuantely,\" \"commited,\" \"estalishment\" and \"consequense.\" You also use an incorrect possessive, as in \"protect all teenagers's future.\" Next, proofread for spelling and apostrophes, and keep a short list of words you misspell so you can check them in future writing.","rationale":"Spelling errors are frequent and some punctuation is incorrect, such as the possessive apostrophe. Errors are widespread across the essay, placing it at limited.","suggestedLevel":"l2","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"Unfortuantely, people who had done any crime or violated any law in the past"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"The curfews is brought out to protect all teenagers's future"}],"uncertainty":"low"}]}
