y can just work so that they can help there families out."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Also would make good money at a early age."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Students would love to finish school in three years because they dont want to keep on going to school."}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"vocabulary","observation":"You communicate your main ideas, but your word choice is limited and often repetitive. 'Early' and 'a early age' appear many times, and general words such as 'good' and 'help out' are used in place of more precise language. Phrases such as 'financially good with money' and 'a good financial job' are unclear. Try more specific vocabulary, such as 'financially stable,' 'earn a steady income,' 'support their families,' or 'enter the workforce,' and vary your wording to avoid repetition.","suggestedLevel":"l2","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"Because, they are not financially good with money."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"They can also start living be them self wants they have a good financial job and out of college at a early age."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Also would make good money at a early age."}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"phraseology","observation":"You use some natural expressions well, such as 'take this chance' and 'get that over with,' which sound natural in English. Other expressions need work. 'At a early age' is a fixed phrase that should be 'at an early age,' and it appears several times. 'Help out there family's' and 'a good financial job' are not standard collocations. Learning common collocations such as 'support their families,' 'secure a stable job,' and 'earn a good salary' would make your writing sound more natural.","suggestedLevel":"l2","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"There are three reasons why students may want to take this chance."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Students may know what they want to become when they are older and would like to start going to college at a early age"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"So graduating a year early may help the students help out there family's."}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"grammar","observation":"Your writing communicates your ideas, but there are several recurring errors. Subject-verb agreement is inconsistent, as in 'Some school district offer programs.' Possessive and pronoun forms are often wrong, such as 'there family' instead of 'their family' and 'it would benefit they' instead of 'it would benefit them.' Articles and noun forms also need attention: 'a early age' should be 'an early age,' and 'these are three good reason' should be 'these are three good reasons.' Check each sentence for agreement, the correct pronoun or possessive form, and singular and plural nouns during revision.","suggestedLevel":"l2","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"Some school district offer programs that allow high school students to graduate in three years instead of the traditional four years."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"First reason is that they may need to help there family out."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"it would benefit they if they could finish high school in three years."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"these are three good reason why students would like to finish high school in three years."}],"uncertainty":"low"},{"criterionId":"conventions","observation":"Your ideas are generally readable, but spelling, punctuation, and capitalisation need attention. 'Dont' should be 'don't,' and 'family's' should be 'families.' 'There' is used where 'their' is needed. The comma in 'Because, they are not financially good with money' is misplaced, and the first sentence of the second paragraph is missing a comma after 'First of all.' Proofreading each sentence for apostrophes, homophones, and commas will make a clear difference to how your writing is received.","suggestedLevel":"l2","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"they dont have to worry about having to go to school"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"So graduating a year early may help the students help out there family's."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Because, they are not financially good with money."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"First of all one reason that it may be good for the students to graduate early"}],"uncertainty":"low"}]}
