 of others."}]},{"criterionId":"vocabulary","observation":"You use clear, everyday words that communicate your ideas, such as \"experience,\" \"interesting,\" and \"benefits.\" To build range, try replacing repeated words like \"fun\" and \"new\" with more precise alternatives (e.g., \"enjoyable,\" \"rewarding,\" \"fresh\"). Also check your spelling of key words such as \"interested\" and \"information,\" since precise vocabulary depends on accurate spelling.","uncertainty":"medium","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"how fun it was"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"experience the fun time that they had"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"that will have benefits"}]},{"criterionId":"phraseology","observation":"You use some useful multi-word expressions, such as \"learn from the experiences of others\" and \"you are not going to regret it,\" which sound natural in English. To develop this further, practise common collocations such as \"take part in\" a school activity or \"gain experience,\" and avoid phrases that sound slightly unnatural, such as \"experience the fun time.\"","uncertainty":"medium","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"I think it is important to learm from the experience of others."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"you are not going to regret it"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"experience the fun time that they had"}]},{"criterionId":"grammar","observation":"Your sentences are mostly understandable, and you use past tense correctly to describe what others did (\"participated,\" \"learned\"). Check a few points: use \"in\" rather than \"on\" with \"a school activity\" and make the noun plural where needed. \"Information\" is uncountable, so it does not take a plural form. Also, \"activity\" should be plural when referring to several activities.","uncertainty":"medium","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"participated on a school activity"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"you might learn some new informations"}]},{"criterionId":"conventions","observation":"Your writing is generally easy to read, but some spelling errors affect clarity. Check the spelling of \"learm,\" \"intrested,\" and \"informations.\" Also remove the space before the comma after \"experienced,\" and add punctuation (such as a full stop or a comma with a conjunction) to separate the long clauses in your second paragraph.","uncertainty":"low","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"I think it is important to learm from the experience of others."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"You can get intrested"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"what they experienced , and you found it interesting."}]}]}
