\" and \"very important,\" and \"problem\" appears very frequently. Try replacing some of these with more precise alternatives, such as \"obstacle,\" \"setback,\" or \"crucial,\" to express your ideas more exactly.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"Almost everyone in the world had a big problem in their life."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"All of these reasons are very important to know."}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"phraseology","observation":"You use some useful expressions, such as \"do your best,\" \"push harder,\" and \"go together.\" Some expressions need correction, though. \"Agree on\" should be \"agree with\" when you mean to accept someone's view, and \"work hard and hard\" is not a standard phrase; \"work harder and harder\" or \"work very hard\" would be more natural. The phrase \"Last but not the least\" is usually written as \"Last but not least.\" Learning common collocations like these will make your writing sound more natural.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"I agree on what he said."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"But they work hard and hard because problems make us work harder."}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"grammar","observation":"There are frequent errors with subject-verb agreement, singular and plural nouns, and verb forms. Examples include \"Problem is not rare this days\" (should be \"Problems are...\"), \"problems is not that bad\", \"Many buisnessman have many problems\" (should be \"businessmen\"), and \"I never seen my brother\" (should be \"I had never seen\" or \"I never saw\"). Also check the third-person forms: \"a person have\" should be \"has,\" and \"problem make us\" should be \"problems make us.\" Reviewing subject-verb agreement and past tense forms will help considerably.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"Problem is not rare this days."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"When a person have a problem of course their going to create/set a goal to complete."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"I never seen my brother since I was 3 years old."}],"uncertainty":"high"},{"criterionId":"conventions","observation":"Your punctuation and spelling need attention. Some common words are misspelt, including \"buisnessman\" and \"Buisness-man.\" Apostrophes are missing in contractions such as \"dont\" and in \"Its,\" which should be \"It's.\" \"Your My Boss\" should be \"You're My Boss\" and should be italicised as a film title. There is a missing space after a comma in \"again,and,\" and the quotation mark placement around Duke Ellington's words needs correcting. Checking your work for these details will make your essay much easier to read.","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"So, I created a goal that I want to see my brother again,and it did happen."},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Like what the movie(Your My Boss) said"}],"uncertainty":"low"}]}
